    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d23">

                <pb facs="0147" n="33" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg33"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/4022a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Sackett</hi>)<anchor n="39" xml:id="d23-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-20T19:00:00-04:00">June 20, 1931—7
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>84. Owing to premature information reaching the press it is necessary for the
                    President to issue a statement for publication tomorrow regarding the proposal
                    to postpone all inter-governmental debts in line with my telegram to you. Please
                    explain this at once to the government.</p>
                <p>I am particularly anxious that this should not interfere with the making of a
                    favorable statement by Hindenburg.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d23-f1" n="39" type="source" xml:id="d23-f1-content">
                <p>First paragraph sent also to the Chargé in Great Britain as Department’s No. 176
                    and to the Ambassador in France as No. 261.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
